{% set c = r.coverage %}
{% set p = r.portfolio %}
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>Cyber Risk Report</title>
<style>
  :root { --ink:#1b1f24; --muted:#5b6470; --line:#dde1e6; --bg:#fafbfc; --card:#fff;
          --accent:#b42318; --accent-soft:#fde8e6; --bar:#d9534f; --ok:#2e7d32; }
  @media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {
    :root { --ink:#e6e8eb; --muted:#9aa4af; --line:#30363d; --bg:#0d1117; --card:#161b22;
            --accent:#ff7b72; --accent-soft:#3a1d1d; --bar:#f0625a; }
  }
  * { box-sizing: border-box; }
  body { margin:0; padding:2rem 1rem; background:var(--bg); color:var(--ink);
         font:15px/1.5 -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, "Segoe UI", Roboto, sans-serif; }
  main { max-width: 1180px; margin: 0 auto; }
  h1 { font-size:1.8rem; margin:0 0 .25rem; }
  h2 { font-size:1.2rem; margin:2.5rem 0 .75rem; padding-bottom:.35rem; border-bottom:1px solid var(--line); }
  h3 { font-size:1rem; margin:1.5rem 0 .5rem; }
  .meta, .note { color:var(--muted); font-size:.85rem; }
  .caveat { background:var(--accent-soft); border-left:3px solid var(--accent); padding:.75rem 1rem; border-radius:4px; margin:1rem 0; font-size:.9rem; }
  .kpis { display:grid; grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit, minmax(200px, 1fr)); gap:.75rem; margin:1rem 0; }
  .kpi { background:var(--card); border:1px solid var(--line); border-radius:8px; padding:1rem; }
  .kpi .label { color:var(--muted); font-size:.8rem; text-transform:uppercase; letter-spacing:.04em; }
  .kpi .value { font-size:1.6rem; font-weight:650; font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums; }
  .kpi .sub { color:var(--muted); font-size:.85rem; }
  .scroll { overflow-x:auto; background:var(--card); border:1px solid var(--line); border-radius:8px; }
  table { border-collapse:collapse; width:100%; font-size:.86rem; }
  th, td { padding:.45rem .6rem; border-bottom:1px solid var(--line); text-align:left; vertical-align:top; }
  th { color:var(--muted); font-weight:600; white-space:nowrap; background:var(--bg); }
  tr:last-child td { border-bottom:0; }
  td.n, th.n { text-align:right; font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums; white-space:nowrap; }
  code { font-size:.8rem; background:var(--bg); padding:.05rem .3rem; border-radius:3px; }
  .badge { display:inline-block; font-size:.7rem; font-weight:600; padding:.05rem .4rem; border-radius:3px; background:var(--accent-soft); color:var(--accent); }
  .bar { height:.55rem; background:var(--bar); border-radius:2px; min-width:1px; }
  .bar-cell { width:22%; min-width:120px; }
  a { color:inherit; }
</style>
</head>
<body>
<main>
<h1>Cyber Risk Quantification Report</h1>
<div class="meta">Generated {{ r.generated_at|datefmt }} · KEV through {{ c.latest_kev_added|datefmt }} · NVD through {{ c.latest_nvd_modified|datefmt }} · Scored {{ c.last_scored|datefmt }} · <a href="/report.md">Markdown</a> · <a href="/docs">API</a></div>

<div class="caveat"><strong>Inherent risk, point estimates.</strong> Figures assume every applicable vulnerability is unpatched and unmitigated. They come from a FAIR-lite model whose constants are documented in <code>docs/assumptions.md</code>, and are meant for ranking and prioritization, not forecasting.</div>

{% if p.riskiest %}
<div class="kpis">
  <div class="kpi"><div class="label">Modeled exposure</div><div class="value">{{ p.total_ale|money }}</div><div class="sub">per year, {{ c.scenarios }} scenarios</div></div>
  <div class="kpi"><div class="label">Riskiest asset</div><div class="value" style="font-size:1.15rem">{{ p.riskiest.asset.name }}</div><div class="sub">{{ p.riskiest.total_ale|money }}/yr · {{ p.riskiest.kev_count }} KEV CVEs</div></div>
  <div class="kpi"><div class="label">Patching top {{ r.remediations|length }} CVEs</div><div class="value">−{{ p.top_remediation_reduction|money }}</div><div class="sub">{{ p.top_remediation_share|pct(0) }} of modeled exposure</div></div>
  <div class="kpi"><div class="label">Applicable CVEs</div><div class="value">{{ c.applicable_cves }}</div><div class="sub">of {{ c.kev }} KEV · {{ c.kev_ransomware }} ransomware-linked</div></div>
</div>
{% else %}
<p>No scenarios are scored yet. Run <code>python -m app.cli pipeline</code>.</p>
{% endif %}

<h2>Risk register by asset</h2>
{% set max_total = (r.assets|map(attribute="total_ale")|max) if r.assets else 0 %}
<div class="scroll"><table>
<tr><th>Asset</th><th>Type</th><th class="n">Tier</th><th class="n">CVEs</th><th class="n">KEV</th><th class="n">P(attack succeeds)</th><th class="n">Loss events/yr</th><th class="n">Loss/event</th><th class="n">ALE/yr</th><th></th><th class="n">P(≥1 loss)</th></tr>
{% for a in r.assets %}
<tr><td><strong>{{ a.asset.name }}</strong></td><td>{{ a.asset.type }}</td><td class="n">{{ a.asset.sensitivity_tier }}</td><td class="n">{{ a.scenario_count }}</td><td class="n">{{ a.kev_count }}</td><td class="n">{{ a.aggregate.p_any|pct }}</td><td class="n">{{ a.expected_loss_events|num(3) }}</td><td class="n">{{ a.aggregate.lm|money }}</td><td class="n"><strong>{{ a.total_ale|money }}</strong></td>
<td class="bar-cell"><div class="bar" style="width:{{ (100 * a.total_ale / max_total) if max_total else 0 }}%"></div></td><td class="n">{{ a.prob_loss_event|pct }}</td></tr>
{% endfor %}
</table></div>
<p class="note">An attacker needs one working vulnerability: P(attack succeeds) = 1 − Π(1 − p<sub>i</sub>); loss events/yr = asset threat frequency × that; loss/event is weighted toward the easiest CVEs; P(≥1 loss) = 1 − e<sup>−events</sup>. Naively summing every scenario would give {{ p.scenario_ale_sum|money }}/yr, which treats each CVE as an independent breach.</p>

<h2>Remediation priorities: what to patch first</h2>
<div class="scroll"><table>
<tr><th class="n">#</th><th>CVE</th><th>Vulnerability</th><th class="n">CVSS</th><th>Flags</th><th>Assets affected</th><th class="n">Standalone ALE/yr</th><th class="n">Reduction if patched alone</th><th>CISA due</th><th>Required action</th></tr>
{% for item in r.remediations %}{% set v = item.vulnerability %}
<tr><td class="n">{{ loop.index }}</td><td><a href="https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/{{ v.cve_id }}">{{ v.cve_id }}</a></td><td>{{ v.vulnerability_name or "" }}</td><td class="n">{{ v.cvss_score|num(1) }}</td>
<td>{% if v.kev_flag %}<span class="badge">KEV</span> {% endif %}{% if v.known_ransomware_use %}<span class="badge">ransomware</span>{% endif %}</td>
<td>{{ item.assets|join(", ") }}</td><td class="n"><strong>{{ item.standalone_ale|money }}</strong></td><td class="n">{{ item.reduction|money }}</td><td>{{ v.kev_due_date|datefmt }}</td><td>{{ v.required_action or "" }}</td></tr>
{% endfor %}
</table></div>
<p class="note">Standalone ALE: how dangerous the hole is on its own. Reduction if patched alone: the actual drop in asset ALE, which is small when an asset has many other exploitable CVEs. That gap signals a systemic fix (upgrade, isolate, replace) rather than one more patch.</p>

<h2>Top {{ r.top_scenarios|length }} risk scenarios</h2>
<div class="scroll"><table>
<tr><th>CVE</th><th>Asset</th><th>Matched on</th><th class="n">CVSS</th><th>KEV</th><th class="n">TEF</th><th class="n">P(exploit)</th><th class="n">LEF</th><th class="n">Primary</th><th class="n">Secondary</th><th class="n">LM</th><th class="n">ALE/yr</th></tr>
{% for s, v, a in r.top_scenarios %}
<tr><td>{{ v.cve_id }}</td><td>{{ a.name }}</td><td><code>{{ s.matched_technology }}</code></td><td class="n">{{ v.cvss_score|num(1) }}</td><td>{% if v.kev_flag %}<span class="badge">KEV</span>{% endif %}</td>
<td class="n">{{ s.tef|num }}</td><td class="n">{{ s.exploit_probability|pct }}</td><td class="n">{{ s.lef|num(3) }}</td><td class="n">{{ s.primary_loss|money }}</td><td class="n">{{ s.secondary_loss|money }}</td><td class="n">{{ s.lm|money }}</td><td class="n"><strong>{{ s.ale|money }}</strong></td></tr>
{% endfor %}
</table></div>
<p class="note">Each scenario scored as if it were the only vulnerability. ALE = LEF × LM · LEF = TEF × P(exploit) · LM = primary + secondary loss.</p>

<h2>Asset detail</h2>
{% for d in r.asset_details %}{% set a = d.summary.asset %}
<h3>{{ a.name }}: {{ d.summary.total_ale|money }}/yr · {{ d.summary.scenario_count }} applicable CVEs</h3>
<p class="note">{{ a.description or "" }} Stack: {% for t in a.technologies %}<code>{{ t }}</code> {% endfor %}</p>
<div class="scroll"><table>
<tr><th>CVE</th><th>Vulnerability</th><th class="n">CVSS</th><th>KEV</th><th class="n">Standalone ALE/yr</th></tr>
{% for s, v, _ in d.scenarios %}
<tr><td>{{ v.cve_id }}</td><td>{{ v.vulnerability_name or "" }}</td><td class="n">{{ v.cvss_score|num(1) }}</td><td>{% if v.kev_flag %}<span class="badge">KEV</span>{% endif %}</td><td class="n">{{ s.ale|money }}</td></tr>
{% endfor %}
</table></div>
{% endfor %}

<h2>How CVSS severity translates to dollars</h2>
<div class="scroll"><table>
<tr><th>Severity</th><th>In KEV?</th><th class="n">Scenarios</th><th class="n">Avg standalone ALE</th><th class="n">Sum standalone ALE</th></tr>
{% for row in r.severity %}
<tr><td>{{ row.severity }}</td><td>{{ "yes" if row.kev_flag else "no" }}</td><td class="n">{{ row.scenarios }}</td><td class="n">{{ row.avg_ale|money }}</td><td class="n">{{ row.total_ale|money }}</td></tr>
{% endfor %}
</table></div>
<p class="note">KEV membership (real exploitation) multiplies exploit probability by {{ r.assumptions.kev_multiplier|num(0) }}×, which is why exploited HIGH CVEs can outrank unexploited CRITICAL ones.</p>

<h2>Weakness classes (CWE)</h2>
<div class="scroll"><table>
<tr><th>CWE</th><th class="n">CVEs</th><th class="n">Sum standalone ALE/yr</th></tr>
{% for row in r.cwes %}
<tr><td><a href="https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/{{ row.cwe[4:] }}.html">{{ row.cwe }}</a></td><td class="n">{{ row.cve_count }}</td><td class="n">{{ row.total_ale|money }}</td></tr>
{% endfor %}
</table></div>

<h2>Methodology and limitations</h2>
<ul>
  <li><strong>FAIR-lite point estimate:</strong> ALE = LEF × LM. Benchmark {{ r.assumptions.benchmark|money }} (IBM/Ponemon <em>Cost of a Data Breach 2024</em> global average; verify before citing). Split {{ r.assumptions.primary_share|pct(0) }} primary / {{ r.assumptions.secondary_share|pct(0) }} secondary.</li>
  <li><strong>Applicability:</strong> CVEs are scored only against assets whose declared stack matches NVD CPE data. An incomplete stack means under-counting.</li>
  <li><strong>Aggregation:</strong> scenarios combine per asset with a "one open door" model (docs/assumptions.md A7), not a plain sum.</li>
  <li><strong>Not modeled:</strong> patch or mitigation status, compensating controls, breaches spreading between assets, uncertainty ranges (Monte Carlo is the planned next stage).</li>
  <li><strong>Coverage:</strong> {{ c.vulnerabilities }} CVEs stored, {{ c.with_cvss }} with CVSS, {{ c.kev }} in KEV, {{ c.kev_without_cvss }} KEV entries unscorable (no NVD vector yet).</li>
</ul>
</main>
</body>
</html>
